"The prognosis is influenced by several documented factors. Favorable findings include a negative surgical margin (0.0), absence of seminal vesicle invasion (0.0), absence of lymphovascular invasion (0.0), and a Gleason 3+4 (ISUP grade group 2) pathology. Countervailing factors include the preoperative PSA of 4.5 and the absence of lymph node removal, resulting in a pNx status, which widens uncertainty regarding nodal status. The biopsy finding of Gleason 3+4 aligns with the surgical specimen. The primary uncertainty lies in the missing postoperative PSA and subsequent trajectory, as previous notes are unavailable. Missing nodal sampling further complicates the assessment of local control. Information regarding postoperative PSA levels and its subsequent trajectory would significantly revise this prognosis. The fixed estimated horizon is 84.76 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 50.86–118.66 months; its coverage has not been validated."
